1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1841 Census entry at Trewellard, St. Just in Penwith:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary White,,70,Independent,In county
2 CONT
2 CONT Margery White,,30,Day Labourer,In county
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary White, widow of Trewellard, made a will on Dec 15, 1845. The will was proved June 17, 1846 and named her dau Margery (exec) and son William, and other dau's Mary (wife of John Johns), Ann (wife of Edmund Trembath), and Elizab
2 CONC eth (wife of Captain John Grenfell). Witnesses were John and Henry Williams.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is the will:
2 CONT
2 CONT This the last Will and Testament of me Mary White of Trewellard in the Parish of St.Just in Penwith in the County of Cornwall.
2 CONT
2 CONT First, I give and bequeath unto my Son William White one large Silver Table Spoon
2 CONT
2 CONT immediately after my death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, I give and bequeath to my daughter Mary the Wife of John Johns of the said parish of
2 CONT
2 CONT St.Just Miner one Small Silver Table Spoon, immediately after my death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, I give and bequeath to my daughter Ann the Wife of Edmund Trembath of the said
2 CONT
2 CONT parish of St.Just, one Silver Punch ladel, immediately after my death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, I give and bequeath to my daughter Elizabeth the Wife of Capt. John Grenfall of the said
2 CONT
2 CONT parish of St.Just Mine Agent, one Silver Sugar Tongs, immediately after my death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also Lastly, All the rest Residue and remainder of all my Goods Chattles and Effects Including
2 CONT
2 CONT all my Annuity or Rent charge that I now hold by virtue of a Covenant from Mr.Nathan White
2 CONT
2 CONT during the life of William Bolitho. I give and bequeath to my daughter Margery, whome I do hereby nominate and appoint whole and sole Executrix and Residuary Legatee of this my last
2 CONT
2 CONT Will and Testament. She paying and discharging all my just Debts and Funeral Charges, and I
2 CONT
2 CONT do hereby revoke all former wills by me made.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Witness whereof I have to this my last Will and Testament Subscribed my name and affixed
2 CONT
2 CONT my seal this Fifteenth day of December in the Year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred
2 CONT
2 CONT and forty five.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed published and declared
2 CONT
2 CONT by the said Mary White as and for her
2 CONT
2 CONT last Will and Testament in the presence of The Sign of
2 CONT
2 CONT us who in her presence and in the presence of each other Mary White
2 CONT
2 CONT subscribed our names.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Williams
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Williams
