1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ote:
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate document states that she is the only child of Catherine Matthews White:
2 CONT
2 CONT This is the Renounce of Catherine White of any claim to the goods of her late Mother Catherine White, who died in 1788.
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine White (Senior) being the Widow of Nathan White.They married 25th.July 1753 at St.Just in Penwith. She being Catherine Matthews before marriage.She was buried on the 4th.of May 1788 at St.Just in Penwith.No will being mad
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT Know All Men by these presents,That I Catherine White of the Parish of Saint Just in the County of Cornwall Spinster the lawfull Daughter and only child of Catherine White late of the same Parish/ Widow deceased/ for diverse good 
2 CONC causes and considerations me thereunto moving have renounced relingquished quitted Claim and refused and by these presents Do renounce relinquish, quitt claim and refuse to take upon me the Burthen of the Administration
2 CONT
2 CONT of the Goods and Chattles, Debts, Rights, Credits and Effects of my said Mother Catherine White deceased And I do hereby desire that the Administration of all and singular the Goods Chattles Debts, Rights, Credits and Effects of m
2 CONC y said Mother deceased may be committed and granted to Elizabeth Matthews of the parish of Morvah in the said County Widow And that this my said renunciation may have its Due Effect, I do hereby authorise and appoint John Wallis G
2 CONC entleman one of the Proctors of the Archdeconry Court of Cornwall or any other Proctor of the same court to Exhibit the same pray the same may be admitted accordingly.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Witness whereof I have hereunto set my Hand and Seal this Seventeenth day of May in twentyeighth Year of the Reign of our Sovereign Lord George the Third and in the year of our Lord one thousand seven hundred and eighty eight.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed
2 CONT
2 CONT and delivered being first duly stampt The sign or mark of
2 CONT
2 CONT In presence of Catherine White
2 CONT
2 CONT Jn.Pearce
