1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burke’s genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry. Vol 2, by John Burke.
2 CONT
2 CONT (As printed in the Gentleman’s Magazine, for January, 1827)
2 CONT
2 CONT A pedigree of the Pawley family, attested by George Owen, York herald, of which a copy is preserved in the College of Arms, is said ‘to have been in the keeping of Mrs. Busvargus, of St. Just in Penwith, 19 March, 1747.’ It commen
2 CONC ces with Stephen Pawley, of Gunwin, in Cornwall, who married Margery, dau. And co-heiress of Ambrose Brea, of Paul, whose son and heir, Stephen Pawley, the eldest son, m. Margery dau. and heir of Robert Tresteane, of Trenowa, by G
2 CONC race dau of Robert Arundell of Camborne, who m. A dau. of William Clopton, of Clopton. co. Warwick, by Elizabeth dau. of Sir Edward Grey, of Whothington. co. Stafford.  The said Stephen Pawley d. 19 Nov 1635, and a handsome table 
2 CONC monument to his memory exists in Lelant Church, containing the arms of Pawley, vis., Or, a lion rampant, sable, on a chief. Dancette, of the second, three mullets, arg. Crest, a unicorn’s head, issuing from a ducal coronet, quarte
2 CONC ring Tresteane.  On another compartment is a shield of the arms of Tresteane, impalling Arundell.  By Margery Brea, he had five sons and five daus.; Hugh Pawley, the oldest son. M. Joan. Dau. of _Searl, and besides Prudence, who m
2 CONC . William Busvargus, had four sons and four daus.  The Pawley family is now represented by that Buck of Biddeford, in consequence of the marriage of John Buck, with Judith, dau. and heir of Hugh Pawley, of Biddeford, merchant, the
2 CONC  descendant of William Pawley, of that place, who was a younger son of Hugh Pawley, of Lelant, a son of Hugh Pawley, by Joan Searle.  Mrs Buck d. 5 Oct. 1739, aged 28, leaving three sons, George, Lewis, and William Buck. – Vide ‘H
2 CONC istory of Biddeford.’
