1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry was a tin miner and in 1855 went to Ishpeming, Michigan.  His wife Honor remained in England with their sons until about 1862.  He worked in the copper mines until he moved to kansas in about 1867.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived on a quarter section (160 acres) in Jackson County about 13 miles northeast of St Marys, Kansas.  They fenced with property with Osage Orange Trees, then his house burned tand the grasshoppers came so he and his two eldes
2 CONC t sons worked in the gold mines in Colorado.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his wife Honor died he went back to England, he met Sarah Elizabeth 'Bess' Day Cyres on the ship back to America in 1905, they married and lived in Emmett Township in Pottawatomic County, Kansas.
