2 ADDR
3 CITY Newlyn East
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1585
2 ADDR
3 CITY Camborne
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 BURI
2 DATE 18 MAR 1585
2 ADDR
3 CITY Camborne
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Arundell was the eldest son of John Arundell by his second wife,  Juliana Erisey. He was born before his parents married and therefore his younger brother John, inherited Trerice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert is named as a "natural son" in his father's will and was left property, the estate of Menadarva in Camborne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Described as an illegitimate son in two deeds and his father's inquisition post mortem.
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''The visitation of the county of Cornwall, in the year 1620 v.9
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/visitationofcoun09vivi
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/visitationofcoun09vivi#page/n19/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 3
2 CONT *'''Robt. Arundell 2 son of S'r John Arundel of Camborne1 = Elizab. Da. of Will'm Clapton Esq. of Stafford
2 CONT **Christopher Arundell of Camborne in com. Cornwall2 = 3Katherine Da. of Will'm Chiverton of Pawle in com. Cornub.4  ....
2 CONT **'''     1 This Robert was a bastard son of Sir John Arundell of Trerice, and is so described by him in two deeds dated 4 Jan., 1 Ed. VI., and 26 Jan., 2 Eliz. Vid Inq. P. M. Sir John Arundell of Trerice. 3 Eliz., No. 23 part 1.
2 CONT **'''     2 Mentioned in the will of John Arundell of Trerice, proved in London 26 Nov., 1580, of which his father Robert was one of the executors. There are several other children of Robert named in this will.
2 CONT *_________________________________
2 CONT *'''Bibliotheca cornubiensis. A catalogue of the writings, both manuscript and printed, of Cornishmen, and of works relating to the county of Cornwall, with biographical memoranda and copious literary references (1874)
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/bibliothecacorn00courgoog
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/bibliothecacorn00courgoog#page/n137/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg. 1041
2 CONT *'''ARUNDELL, ROBERT (natural son of sir John Arundell of Trerice) Settled at Menadarva, Camborne, m. Elizabeth, dau. of Will. Clapton of Stafford.
2 CONT *'''   Grant to sir J. Tyrrel and R. Goulds of the ward and marriage of Robert Arundell, son and heir of John Arundell, with the keeping of all lands. Harl. MSS. 433, art. 651.
2 CONT *_____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitations Arundells of Lanherne (start of Pedigree)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Trerice Arundells Visitations 1 & 2 The Menderva Arundells leading onto William Arundell Yeo
2 CONT
2 CONT The Menederva Arundells
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Robert 15 Arundell (Sir John 14 , Sir John 13 , Sir John 12 , Nicholas 11 , Sir John 10 , Nicholas 9 , Ralph 8 , Ralph 7 , Sir Oliver 6 , Sir Renfry 5 , Humphrey 4 de Arundell, Richard 3 , Gilbert 2 , Roger 1 ) He married Eliz
2 CONC abeth Clapton .
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Robert Arundell and Elizabeth Clapton is:
2 CONT
2 CONT +16 i. Christopher 16 Arundell.
2 CONT
2 CONT This Robert Arundell (of Menadarva, in Camborne) was apparently a bastard son of Sir John Arundell of Trerice (died 1560-61, 3 Eliz): see a note in the Gentleman's Magazine, Sept 1829, pp. 215-16 (copy in AR/29/9). He was left sha
2 CONC red interests on many of his father's properties and mentioned in his will and that of his half brother Sir John Arundell.
2 CONT
2 CONT This deed solves the problem of Charles Henderson, A History of the Parish of Constantne in Cornwall, p.165: 'How Treworvack passed from the Arundells of Trerice to the Arundells of Lanherne, between 1558 and 1659, is very strange
2 CONC . The two families were very remotely (if at all) related to one another. However, Robert;s maternal grandmother was Jane Grenville and her sister Katherine married Sir John Arundell of Lanherne.
2 CONT
2 CONT (27 Eliz) Bargain and sale, Robert Arundell of Menaderva, esquire, and Christopher Arundell his son and heir apparent = (1)-(2). Sir John Arundell of Lanherne, knight = (3). Consideration: £45 paid by (3) to (1)-(2). 91)-(2) to (3
2 CONC ), their messuages, lands, tenements, rents, reversions, remainders, services, meadows, pastures, feedings, moors, waste grounds, etc., in Trewheverack (parish of Constentyn), together with all writings, evidences, etc.; for (3) a
2 CONC nd his heirs to hold for ever, to his sole use, of the chief lords of the fee, by rents and services due and accustomed. Covenant that the premises are free from encumbrances, except for the chief rent and service due to the chief
2 CONC  lords; covenant of peaceable occupation. Signatures of (1)-(2). [dorse] Note of sealing and delivery. 2 seals, of (1)-(2). Trewheverack [Treworvack in Constantine; tenement of Prospidnick manor] 1584, 10th Dec
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift and feoffment to use Robert Arundell de Menaderva, esquire, and Christopher Arundell his son and heir = (1)-(2). John Arundell of Lanherne, knight = (3)(1)-(2) to (3), in part performance of an agreement made between them, al
2 CONC l their messuages, lands, tenements, rents, reversions, remainders, services, etc., in Trewheverack (parish of Constentyn); for (3) and his heirs to hold for ever, to his sole use, of the chief lords of the fee, by rents and servi
2 CONC ces due and accustomed. Warranty. Appointment of William Williams and Edward Vivian as attorneys to deliver seisin. Signatures of (1)-(2). [dorse] Note of sealing and delivery. 2 seals [of (1)-(2)]. Trewheverack [Treworvack in Con
2 CONC stantine; tenement of Prospidnick manor]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1585, Easter term Final concord; with counterpart. John Arundell, knight, claimant = (1). Robert Arundell esquire, Elizabeth his wife, Christopher Arundell esquire and Katherine his wife, deforciants = (2)-(5). 1 messuage, 2 tofts
2 CONC , 2 gardens, 60 acres of land, 10 acres of meadow, 20 acres of pasture and 40 acres of furze and heath in Trewheverack (Constentyn); (2)-(5) acknowledge them to be the right of (1) as by their gift, and quitclaimed them to him and
2 CONC  his heirs for ever. Warranty by (2)-(5) against themselves, their heirs, and the heirs of John Arundell of Trerice, knight (deceased). For this (1) gave £41 to (2)-(5).
