1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Trembath, yeoman of Chyrose, made a will Feb 20, 1806. The will was proved May 14, 1806 and named his wife Rebekah, daughters Mary, Rebecka, Elizabeth, Hannah, and Honour; and sons Richard and james. Witnesses were Francis
2 CONC  Thomas (must be relative of his wife) and Wm Shakerley (his brother in law...not sure how).Possible parents and DOB from the IGI are:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Trembath and Mary Stone.....list DOB as March 10, 1743
2 CONT
2 CONT Another entry lists Christening date as March 10, 1744, father James Trembath.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both entries list Place of Birth as St. Just
2 CONT
2 CONT There are some other possibilities...need to look at original films to see where they really lived (i.e. Trewellard, Boscaswell, etc.)...which will help narrow it down.
