1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Margaret and James had a falling-out in their marriage in 1839, however, they got back together after a short seperation.  After James had died, and her sons had gotten a bit older, Margaret emigrated to Australia 
2 CONC on the Great Britain.  She arrived in Melbourne on April,1866.  With her were her sons Thomas (20), Hugh (18), daughter Grace (1851-1925) (after 1870, Mrs Henry Leggo) and grandson John Veale (15) (Lavinia's son).  In 1869, a Marg
2 CONC aret Trezise (born in Cornwall) married James Caugherty in Victoria.  I suspect this is her.  I now no longer believe this.  James died at about 40 and he was married in his mid-twenties when Margaret was in her mid fifties.  Anot
2 CONC her clue that I have found is that in April 1881 John Veale (Margaret's grandson) as secretary of the Collman and Tachii Freehold Tribute Company was advertising that 2 shares owned by Margaret in that company would be auctioned b
2 CONC ecause she didn't pay when called upon.  I guess John would have known where his grandmother was if she was still alive (unless the shares were rubbish and she had abandoned them).
