1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MARGARET CHIRGWIN   (1641-1695)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Chirgwin was the wife of Thomas Taylor and daughter of Edward Chirgwin and Cheston Edwards and was christened at Sancreed on 10 April 1641.  She was widowed when she was 45 in 1686 and died nine years later and buried at 
2 CONC Sancreed on 11 June 1695. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The inventory of her assets totalled £32  11 shillings and 2 pence with the major items being her property valued at £10 and 3 cows, 2 steers and 9 horses.  The description of the livestock included “one old gray horse, one old gr
2 CONC ay nagg valued att £1  10 shillings”.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret’s will was made in 1691.  It left her son-in-law Richard Pearce and daughter Margaret £3 and discharged Richard a debt of £2 for a horse sold to him.  Mary, the daughter of Richard Pearce was left £1.  Margaret’s unmarrie
2 CONC d children, Richard, then aged 22, Cheston, Grace, Catherine, then aged 11 and Jane, then aged 9, were left £5 each to be paid when they turned 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT The rest of her goods and chattels were left to the youngest child, Thomas, aged 6, who was also appointed sole executor.  Five trustees were appointed to act if Thomas was a minor at her death, which he was as Margaret died four 
2 CONC years after completing her will. Margaret could not write and signed with her mark which resembled cricket stumps and bails.
