0 @N6000000004671811419@ NOTE Thomas Grenfield, St Just in Penwith, Cornwall, 9th October 1708 - Inventory
1 CONT
1 CONT A true and perfect inventory of all the goods and chattells of Thomas Grenfield late of the parish of St.Just in Penwith who dyed the 14th. day of August 1708 and was buried the 16th. of said August taken and appraised by us whose
1 CONC  names are hereunto subscribed this 9th. day of October 1708.
1 CONT
1 CONT Impris:-
1 CONT
1 CONT His wearing apparell and money in his pocket                         01 10  00
1 CONT
1 CONT Eight pewter platters          00  12  00
1 CONT
1 CONT Nine pewter dishes Flagon Candlestick and Cup                     00  04 06
1 CONT
1 CONT One iron crock one brass crock and one brandiron                 00  18 06
1 CONT
1 CONT Three pans and a skillett        01  17  06
1 CONT
1 CONT Timber ware with ye cupboard bedstead and chest
1 CONT
1 CONT and old table board and forme   02  00  00
1 CONT
1 CONT Two coverlets a blanket two payer of sheets feather bed and
1 CONT
1 CONT boulster and pillow in all        02  10  00
1 CONT
1 CONT One cow heifer and calfe      03  01  00
1 CONT
1 CONT One old mare two piggs and 4 ews 01  10  00
1 CONT
1 CONT various implements lumber trade and goods forgotten              00  05 00
1 CONT
1 CONT ------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT in all                   14  08 06
1 CONT
1 CONT John Ustick
1 CONT
1 CONT Hen.Ustick
0 @N6000000004671811372@ NOTE John Granvill, St Just in Penwith, Cornwall, 10th December 1741 - Will
1 CONT
1 CONT In the name of God Amen I John Granvill of the Parrish of St.Just in the County of Cornwall being verry sick and Weake butt Blessed be God of perfect mind and memory and calling to mind the Mortallity of this Life knowing that itt
1 CONC  is Appointed for all men once to Die doo make and ordaine this my Last Will and Testament and principally and first of all I recommend and bequeath my soull into the hands of Allmighty God that gave itt and my Boddey to the Earth
1 CONC  to be Buried in a Christian Like and decent manner at the discretion of my Executrix and for the wordly goods that God has been pleased to Endow me with I give and bequeath in manner and form following.
1 CONT
1 CONT Item
1 CONT
1 CONT First I give unto my Daughter Margrett Mathews the Sum of Twenty Three Pounds to be paid her twelve months after my decease also one fetther bed one Boulster and one pillow all of fetthers.
1 CONT
1 CONT 2ly. I give my Daughter Loveday Ankerwis The sum of ten pounds to be paid her Twelve months after my decease And my Right in Wheale Carne in Wm.pegollys (?) work that is to say one ½ deale in thirteen deales of Adventure also one 
1 CONC ½ deale in fourteen of the Trubbitt.
1 CONT
1 CONT 3ly. I give my Grandson Jn.Ankerwis The sum of ten pounds to be paid him when my Executrix Shall Think Fitt.
1 CONT
1 CONT 4ly. I give my Son in Law Thomas Ankerwis my best sut of clothes.
1 CONT
1 CONT 5ly. and Lastly I make my Wife Elizabeth my full Executrix of all the remainder of my Goods and Chattells waht soo ever moveable and unmoveable. Witness my hand and seale The 10th. Day of December 1741
1 CONT
1 CONT Signes Sealled and
1 CONT
1 CONT Declared in presents of us
1 CONT
1 CONT James Reynolds
1 CONT
1 CONT The signe of Marey Reynolds                             The signe and seale of
1 CONT
1 CONT John Granvill
0 @N6000000004671811401@ NOTE Loveday Grenfield and her husband Thomas Ankerwis were first cousins once removed.
0 @N6000000004658060249@ NOTE Geoff McKee has her as christened on July 28, 1705 to William Matthew andCheston Trembath, born in Morvah.
0 @N6000000004658060275@ NOTE Morvah Con Eng Bur. From St Just.
0 @N6000000004658060312@ NOTE Geoff McKee has the year of birth as 1736/37
0 @N6000000004658060827@ NOTE The 1871 census has a No. 163 at Fore Street, St. Just
1 CONT      Jane Trembath Head of household, unmarried, age 67, retired dom.servant, blind, born in Morvah.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1871 census for Chaple Street, St. Just has a Jane Trembath, age 76,gen servant, born in Morvah, boarder with Nicholas G. Williams and family.
0 @N6000000004658058830@ NOTE 1841 Census at Trevegean, St. Just in Penwith:
1 CONT William Trembath,45,,Tin Miner,In county
1 CONT Honor Trembath,,45,,In county
1 CONT William Trembath,25,,Tin Miner,In county
1 CONT Ambrose Trembath,20,,Tin Miner,In county
1 CONT John Trembath,15,,Tin Miner,In county
