1 CONT James Trembath,5,,,In county
0 @N6000000004658060939@ NOTE In 1841 she was living with her son Charles, age 9, Thomas Trembath age40 (her brother) and William Nankervis age 70 (probably her uncle)
0 @N6000000004658060145@ NOTE !Morvah is on the Cornish coast, near Pendeen and north of St. Just-in-Penwith, Cornwall, England.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1841 Cornwall census for St. Just in Penwith, taken June 1841 lis ts:
1 CONT Hugh Trembath age 40, miner, b. 1801
1 CONT Jane, age 42, b. 1799
1 CONT Hugh, age 14
1 CONT John, age 15
1 CONT Mary, age 13
1 CONT William, age 8
1 CONT Elizabeth, age 6
1 CONT Thomas (&#00063;), age 3
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Witness for his death was John Borlase...he was also the informer ofdeath, and is listed as son-in-law, of Sebastapool.
0 @N6000000004658060111@ NOTE I suspect that this Edmund was a member of the Trewellard MethodistChapel. In the "Trewellard Methodist Church 1833-1983" by E.C. CoraCollins, on page 7 there is the following listing:
1 CONT
1 CONT The March 1859 list of sums still owed on money lent for the building ofthe Chapel
1 CONT      Edmund Trembath     85 pounds
1 CONT      Thomas Grose   50
1 CONT      John Stevens   45
1 CONT      John Grose     30
1 CONT      John Rodda     10
1 CONT      William Thomas 25
1 CONT      Henry Stevens  10
